~ start
do SignalManager.cutscene_started.emit()
Amelia: Here's the kitchen breaker box.
Theodore: My fuzzy mitts won't work well with wires. You try to fix it.
Theodore: The Instruction Panel has a few conditions to consider thanks to the terrible wiring job.
Theodore: Left click to flip breaker switches until they are properly set. 
Theodore: The Master Switch is the last one that needs to be selected to get the wires ready for connections.
Theodore: Each top wire has a matching bottom wire that needs to be connected up.
Theodore: Left click the end of each wire to select/deselect that wire. Selecting another wire after will make the connection.
Theodore: If you see sparks flying, you’re on the right track! 
Theodore: But if you make an incorrect connection, the wires will short and the breaker will trip…
Theodore: That means you have to go reset the switches on the breaker before taking another go at the wires.
Theodore: If you can get all those wires connected up we should be able to get power to the Kitchen and Living Room!
Amelia: ... [wait = 1] Oh is that all?
Theodore: Look, I know that sounds like a lot but don’t worry, I’ll be right here with you and we will go nice and slow-
do SignalManager.kitchen_night_light_out.emit()
Theodore: Change of plans...
Theodore: I'll hold off the shadows with my [wave amp=15 freq=5]POWERFUL[/wave] aura.
Amelia: *His steely stare reassures you that he can now navigate freely and use the [wave amp=15 freq=5]INTERACT[/wave] key to blast away the shadows.*
do GameManager.kitchen_puzzle = true
do SignalManager.puzzle_mode.emit()
do SignalManager.activate_enemy_spawner.emit()
#Add puzzle start/teddy combat signal
do SignalManager.cutscene_ended.emit()
do SignalManager.dialogue_ended.emit()
=> END
